# p5 mcp discover (the wire read at ~5 s, between the third try and the fourth -- 1+2+4 s of
# backoff -- and `/mcp show` given 4 s, which fx answers once its next try is over): a stdio server whose `server/discover` result lists only near misses
# of the client's versions -- escapes around "2026-07-28", a 64 KiB string -- with
# instructions that are terminal escapes (p5-mcp-discover-stdio.ts `hostile`). fx v0.0.16
# keeps none of it (a list is a mask over its own versions, era.zig:28-37@481104fd): no
# shared version, "it supports no MCP version fx speaks", retrying. Nothing the server
# wrote reaches the screen.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-hostile-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-hostile-profile.json
gateway p5-mcp-hello.json
wait 5
home wire
type /mcp show fixture
key Enter
wait 4
snap show
